Title: Evian Championship: England's Lottie Woad goes close as Grace Kim wins first major title
Date: 2025-07-13
Firsthand information: {'Speaker': [{'Speaker': 'Lottie Woad', 'Text': "Is there even any point, she's not making six.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 6, 'StartChar': 122, 'EndChar': 164}}, {'Speaker': 'Lottie Woad', 'Text': "I'm going to discuss it with my family and coaches,", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 14, 'StartChar': 1, 'EndChar': 51}}, {'Speaker': 'Lottie Woad', 'Text': "It has always been in my dreams to play on the LPGA Tour and I'm grateful for the opportunities of the programme.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 15, 'StartChar': 1, 'EndChar': 108}}, {'Speaker': 'Lottie Woad', 'Text': 'I was trying to be in contention and winning this, so it will be the same there,', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 17, 'StartChar': 1, 'EndChar': 73}}], 'Description': [{'Description': 'Australian Grace Kim eventually triumphed in France, holing a 12-foot eagle putt on the second extra playing of the 18th hole, to beat her good friend Atthaya Thitikul in a play-off to claim her first major title.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 3, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 169}}, {'Description': 'Kim also eagled the 18th to get into the play-off after Thitikul missed an eight-foot birdie putt that would have seen her win a maiden major.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 4, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 120}}, {'Description': "Woad, who won last week's Irish Open, would also have been in the play-off had she not earlier raced a 10-foot birdie putt past the hole as she posted a sensational seven-under 64 to finish on 13 under par and set the clubhouse target.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 5, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 197}}, {'Description': 'She went to the driving range to hit some balls and keep herself loose but when Thailand\'s Thitikul birdied the 17th to get to 14 under, with just the par-five 18th to play, Woad smiled as she said to her caddie: "Is there even any point, she\'s not making six."', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 6, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 164}}, {'Description': 'Her playing partner Kim then knocked in a two-foot putt for a three as she picked up four shots in her closing four holes to also reach 14 under.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 8, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 128}}, {'Description': 'The players both had birdies when they first replayed the 18th, Kim knocking in a 30-yard chip, before the Australian again got down in three shots to take the title when they played it again.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 9, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 174}}, {'Description': "She picked up two points for finishing in the top 25 in a major and that takes her to 20 overall. That is the magic number on the LPGA's Elite Amateur Pathway which earns her a spot on the LPGA Tour should she want it though she can also defer.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 12, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 209}}], 'Image': [{'ID': 'image_1', 'Caption': 'Lottie Woad reacts to missing a 10-foot birdie putt on the 18th at the Evian Championship'}]}
